  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `adaptive::star::Star::new` cleans each opened row loop before the star laws read it. The new function `denoised` drops a vertex that is less than 1e-5 mm from the last vertex kept.\n- The bore pin `BORE_PIN` in `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs` moves to `(1642, 1614, 300)`. The old pin stays as `BORE_PIN_BEFORE_4010`, and each platform pin test rejects it. The unmeasured-platform band is centred on the new pin with the same half-widths.\n- New fixture: `crates/motion/tests/fixtures/bore_z15_center.txt`. It holds the Z 15 center area of the user's bore (328 vertices), recorded from the 3-D ladder.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/4010-bore-level-plan.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe Z 15 and Z 5 levels give the planner a 328-vertex disc outline. The opening of this outline at R2.5 keeps 20 edges that are 1 or 2 Clipper units long (1.4e-6 to 2.2e-6 mm). Integer rounding turns each of these edges back about the pole.\n\n- `radial` reads such an edge as a shadow.\n- `disc_in_kernel` reads the line of the edge as a wall through the area.\n\nSo the star cell was refused and the growth rings planned the disc. The 128-vertex outline of Z 10 and Z 0 has no such edges, so those levels kept the morph spiral. A probe in the planner showed this on each level:\n\n- 328 points: row 0 fails, so the growth rings plan it (`Grown::Done`).\n- 128 points: a star cell, so the morph spiral plans it.\n\n## Readings (macOS arm64, release)\n\n| Level | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Z 15, Z 5 | 1933 planar feeds, 918 arcs, 999.92 mm | 410 planar feeds, 78 arcs, 330.07 mm |\n| Z 10, Z 0 | 397 planar feeds, 72 arcs, 334.31 mm | no change |\n| Whole path | (4688, 4660, 1980) | (1642, 1614, 300) |\n\nZ 15 and Z 5 now reach the wall at y -7.498 (before: 0.153 mm short in -Y). The path verifies clean with no fallback and no budget note. On unchanged upstream main `498382c8e`, macOS read `(4688, 4660, 1980)`. This is the same triple that Windows and Linux read.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pins (in `camcraft-motion` lib, `machining2d::adaptive::tests`):\n  - `the_users_z15_bore_is_one_star_cell`\n  - `the_users_z15_bore_plans_the_short_spiral` (the walk is less than 500 mm, it does not cross itself, and the rest is under `HSM_REST_MAX`)\n- Red before the fix: yes. Both failed on unchanged code with \"the bore's walk is 1146.46 mm\". The note was the same plan-B corner note, at (5.30, -5.30).\n- Mutation: I put back `star.rs` from `upstream/main`, and the two pins went red. I restored the fix, and the two pins went green.\n- `pocket3d_hsm` in release with `--include-ignored`: the bore test and all the pin and band tests pass. `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` fails at its `known-fail #1950` assert line, as it did before.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base 498382c8e`: 172 steps, 0 failed. This includes `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base 498382c8e`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog suites ran green in the quick gate, and no `*.nc`, `*.cl` or catalog file changed. Only the count pin of `pocket3d_hsm` changed, as given above.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows x86_64 and Linux x86_64 are not measured after the fix. Before the fix they read the same triple as macOS, so the pin follows the macOS reading. Their next run confirms it or adds a platform triple.\n- No full heavy lanes. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a `P3` PR no heavy step. I ran the targeted heavy bore test in release (given above).\n- No probe of the reading before the PR #3802 mesh (Z 10 on the long plan). I expect the same cause, but I did not check it.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/` or `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs`.\n\nChangelog: HSM Adaptive no longer cuts a round 3D Pocket level with a plan three times too long when the outline has offset rounding noise (the bore levels now take the short spiral).\n\nFixes #4010\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
